-- title:
--   Rational function field from a prescribed transcendental element with algebraic remainder
-- statement:
--   For a field extension E/k and an element y transcendental over k, construct an intermediate field K and an injective K-algebra map from RatFunc K into E that sends X to y, with E algebraic over RatFunc K under the induced algebra structure. This isolates the transcendence-basis, evaluation embedding, and algebraicity work needed by the parent. In the boundary case where the transcendence basis consists only of y, K is k; no characteristic or algebraic-closedness condition is needed. A proof route extends {y} to a transcendence basis S, takes K generated by S minus {y}, proves y remains transcendental over K using independence of S, and extends evaluation at y to the rational function field. Algebraicity of E over the field generated by S then gives algebraicity over the embedded RatFunc K. The remaining core is formalizing the intermediate-field identification and algebraicity transfer.

import Mathlib.FieldTheory.FinTrdeg
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.RatFunc.AsPolynomial
import Mathlib.RingTheory.EssentialFiniteness

theorem OAI.PiExponent.FormalInterpolation.exists_rational_function_field_with_algebraic_remainder
    (k E : Type) [Field k] [Field E] [Algebra k E]
    (y : E) (hy : Transcendental k y) :
    ∃ (K : IntermediateField k E) (f : RatFunc K →ₐ[K] E),
      f RatFunc.X = y ∧ Function.Injective f ∧
      (letI : Algebra (RatFunc K) E := f.toRingHom.toAlgebra
       Algebra.IsAlgebraic (RatFunc K) E) := by sorry
